-- Employment Insurance Act (S.C. 1996, c. 23), the part written by piece ei6: Part VIII.4 (the Employment Insurance
-- Emergency Response Benefit), Part VIII.5 and Part VIII.6 (temporary measures), Part IX (transitional provisions and
-- coming into force) and the Schedules -- THE SEAT LAYER. Written by piece ei6 (Sonnet 5.5) on 2026-10-24.
-- Text: the unofficial plain-text rendering of the Justice Laws consolidation current to 2026-09-30; nothing here is
-- claimed to be verified against the official text.
--
-- SEAT: a person who has lost work, or cannot work because of sickness, pregnancy, caring for a child or a family
-- member, or who is self-employed or a fisher, and asks whether they qualify for Employment Insurance benefits, how
-- many hours or weeks they need, how much they would receive and for how long, and what they must do or tell the
-- Commission. Officials have no seat: the Commission and the Minister appear only as what the person is owed or exposed to.
--
-- PLAIN INPUTS. Every question takes plain inputs -- yes/no, numbers, dates and a few choices -- one for each fact the
-- person can state, each with an @desc worded as the person would be asked. The records and BOOLEANs the layer-1
-- modules expect are built inside each question, in its WHERE, from those answers, and the SAME module rule is
-- then called; no rule is restated here. Where a layer-1 rule has a parameter that records the Commission's judgment
-- ("the Commission considers ..."), the question asks it as a fact about what the Commission has decided.
--
-- THE DAYS. Most of this part of the Act is time-limited (2020 to 2021, or 1996 to 1997). A question that depends on
-- a date asks for it. The cessation days of ss 153.14 and 153.196 depend on whether an Interim Order was repealed
-- earlier, which a person cannot state: these questions assume it was not (the seat passes NOTHING), so a repeal
-- before the days the text gives would change the answers (NOTES.md, fork F-ei6-9).
-- A rate of unemployment is asked in per cent (7.5 for 7.5%) and divided by 100 here; hours and weeks are whole numbers.
-- The seat's only own names are the two kinds of choice below and their translators, which turn a choice into the Part
-- and section number the text names.
--
-- Where the layer-1 rule returns a MAYBE, NOTHING means that the section does not apply to this person, so the
-- section of the Act outside this piece decides (pieces ei1 to ei5), or that the text does not answer.

§ `Choices the person makes`

-- The kind of benefit, as the person would name it, translated into the Part of the Act and the number of the section
-- that provides it (the sections are those named in ss 153.5(3) and 12 of the Act: 21 sickness, 22 maternity, 23 parental,
-- 23.1 to 23.3 caring, 24 work-sharing, 152.03 sickness for the self-employed; Part VIII for fishers). For regular
-- benefits and the other benefits of Part I the text names no section outside 21 to 24, so section 12 stands for them.
DECLARE `ei6 seat Kind of benefit` IS ONE OF
    `ei6 seat regular benefits`
    `ei6 seat sickness benefits for an employee (section 21)`
    `ei6 seat maternity benefits (section 22)`
    `ei6 seat parental benefits (section 23)`
    `ei6 seat caring for a family member or a critically ill child or adult (sections 23.1 to 23.3)`
    `ei6 seat work-sharing benefits (section 24)`
    `ei6 seat sickness benefits for a self-employed person (section 152.03)`
    `ei6 seat other benefits for a self-employed person (Part VII.1)`
    `ei6 seat benefits for a fisher (Part VIII)`

GIVEN kind IS A `ei6 seat Kind of benefit`
GIVETH A `Part of the Act`
DECIDE `ei6 seat the Part under which the kind of benefit is provided` IS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `ei6 seat sickness benefits for a self-employed person (section 152.03)` THEN `Part VII.1`
    WHEN `ei6 seat other benefits for a self-employed person (Part VII.1)` THEN `Part VII.1`
    WHEN `ei6 seat benefits for a fisher (Part VIII)` THEN `Part VIII`
    OTHERWISE `Part I`

GIVEN kind IS A `ei6 seat Kind of benefit`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `ei6 seat the number of the section under which the kind of benefit is provided` IS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `ei6 seat regular benefits` THEN 12
    WHEN `ei6 seat sickness benefits for an employee (section 21)` THEN 21
    WHEN `ei6 seat maternity benefits (section 22)` THEN 22
    WHEN `ei6 seat parental benefits (section 23)` THEN 23
    WHEN `ei6 seat caring for a family member or a critically ill child or adult (sections 23.1 to 23.3)` THEN 23.1
    WHEN `ei6 seat work-sharing benefits (section 24)` THEN 24
    WHEN `ei6 seat sickness benefits for a self-employed person (section 152.03)` THEN 152.03
    WHEN `ei6 seat other benefits for a self-employed person (Part VII.1)` THEN 152.05
    WHEN `ei6 seat benefits for a fisher (Part VIII)` THEN 8

-- The Part of the Act that a provision cited in s 153.6 is in, as the person would name it.
DECLARE `ei6 seat Instrument of a provision` IS ONE OF
    `ei6 seat the Employment Insurance Act`
    `ei6 seat the Employment Insurance Regulations`

§ `Part VIII.4 - the Employment Insurance Emergency Response Benefit (March 15 to October 3, 2020)`

-- The group applies only if you claimed, or could have claimed, the emergency response benefit in 2020, or are asked to
-- repay it: ask "Did this happen to you?" before showing it.

-- s 153.5. A "claimant" of the benefit is a person described by any one of paragraphs (a) to (d).
@export Am I a claimant for the Employment Insurance Emergency Response Benefit (s 153.5)?
GIVEN `I stopped working, whether as an employee or self-employed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you stop working, whether you were employed or self-employed?
      `I stopped working for reasons related to COVID-19` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it for reasons related to COVID-19 (the coronavirus disease 2019)?
      `a benefit period could have been established for me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Could a benefit period for Employment Insurance benefits have been established for you?
      `the day on which it could have been established` IS A DATE @desc On what day could that benefit period have been established? (a date; any date if you answered no above)
      `the kind of benefit` IS A `ei6 seat Kind of benefit` @desc Which kind of Employment Insurance benefit was it, or was paid to you?
      `I am unable to start working for reasons related to COVID-19` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you unable to start working for reasons related to COVID-19?
      `a benefit of that kind was paid or payable to me from December 29, 2019 to October 3, 2020` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was a benefit of that kind paid to you, or payable to you, at some time from December 29, 2019 to October 3, 2020?
      `my benefit period ended in that period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did your benefit period end between December 29, 2019 and October 3, 2020?
      `all those benefits were paid to me in that period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were all of those benefits paid to you between December 29, 2019 and October 3, 2020?
      `some of those benefits could not be paid to me because of the maximum` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Could some of those benefits not be paid to you because you had reached a maximum (subsection 12(6) of the Act, or subsection 8(18) of the Employment Insurance (Fishing) Regulations)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I a claimant for the Employment Insurance Emergency Response Benefit` IF
    `s 153.5(2) claimant within the meaning of Part VIII.4` `paragraph (a)` `paragraph (b)` `paragraph (c)` `paragraph (d)`
    WHERE
        `paragraph (a)` MEANS
            `s 153.5(2)(a) claimant who ceases working for reasons related to COVID-19` `I stopped working, whether as an employee or self-employed` `I stopped working for reasons related to COVID-19`
        `paragraph (b)` MEANS
                `a benefit period could have been established for me`
            AND `s 153.5(2)(b) claimant who could have had a benefit period established` `the day on which it could have been established`
                  (`s 153.5(3)(a) the benefit is referred to in paragraph (2)(b)` (`ei6 seat the Part under which the kind of benefit is provided` `the kind of benefit`) (`ei6 seat the number of the section under which the kind of benefit is provided` `the kind of benefit`))
        `paragraph (c)` MEANS
            `s 153.5(2)(c) claimant who is unable to start working after benefits under Part I`
                `I am unable to start working for reasons related to COVID-19`
                (`a benefit of that kind was paid or payable to me from December 29, 2019 to October 3, 2020`
                 AND `s 153.5(3)(b) the benefit is referred to in paragraph (2)(c)` (`ei6 seat the Part under which the kind of benefit is provided` `the kind of benefit`) (`ei6 seat the number of the section under which the kind of benefit is provided` `the kind of benefit`))
                `my benefit period ended in that period`
                `all those benefits were paid to me in that period`
                `some of those benefits could not be paid to me because of the maximum`
        `paragraph (d)` MEANS
            `s 153.5(2)(d) claimant who is unable to start working after benefits under Part VIII`
                `I am unable to start working for reasons related to COVID-19`
                (`a benefit of that kind was paid or payable to me from December 29, 2019 to October 3, 2020`
                 AND `s 153.5(3)(c) the benefit is referred to in paragraph (2)(d)` (`ei6 seat the Part under which the kind of benefit is provided` `the kind of benefit`))
                `my benefit period ended in that period`
                `all those benefits were paid to me in that period`
                `some of those benefits could not be paid to me because of the maximum`

-- s 153.6. Which other provisions apply to a claim for the benefit.
@export Does a given provision of the Act or the Regulations apply to my claim for the Employment Insurance Emergency Response Benefit (s 153.6)?
GIVEN `the instrument the provision is in` IS A `ei6 seat Instrument of a provision` @desc Is the provision in the Employment Insurance Act or in the Employment Insurance Regulations?
      `the Part of the Act that holds the provision` IS A `Part of the Act` @desc Which Part of the Act is the provision in? (for a provision of the Regulations, answer Part I: it is not read)
      `the number of the section` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the number of the section? (for example 44, or 112.1)
      `the provision is a subsection` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a subsection of that section (such as 112(3)), not the whole section?
      `the number of the subsection` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the number of the subsection? (0 if you answered no above)
      `it is a definition set out in subsection 2(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it one of the definitions in subsection 2(1) of the Act?
      `a contrary intention appears` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the provision itself show that it is meant to apply to this benefit?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does a given provision apply to my claim for the Employment Insurance Emergency Response Benefit` IF
    `s 153.6 the provision applies in respect of a claim for the emergency response benefit` `the provision` `it is a definition set out in subsection 2(1)` `a contrary intention appears`
    WHERE
        `the provision` MEANS
            `ei6 Provision cited in section 153.6` OF (`the instrument the provision is in` EQUALS `ei6 seat the Employment Insurance Regulations`), `the Part of the Act that holds the provision`, `the number of the section`, (IF `the provision is a subsection` THEN JUST `the number of the subsection` ELSE NOTHING)

-- s 153.8(1), (2). A claim is for a two-week period that starts on a Sunday and falls within March 15 to October 3, 2020,
-- and is made by December 2, 2020.
@export May I make a claim for the Emergency Response Benefit for this two-week period (s 153.8)?
GIVEN `I am a claimant for the benefit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a claimant for the Emergency Response Benefit? (see the question on who is a claimant)
      `the first day of the two-week period` IS A DATE @desc What is the first day of the two-week period you want to claim for? (a date; it must be a Sunday)
      `I make the claim in the form and manner the Minister has established` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you making the claim in the form and manner the Minister has established?
      `the day on which I make the claim` IS A DATE @desc On what day do you make the claim? (a date)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I make a claim for the Emergency Response Benefit for this two-week period` IF
        `s 153.8(1) the claimant may make a claim for the two-week period`
            `I am a claimant for the benefit`
            `I make the claim in the form and manner the Minister has established`
            (`s 153.8(1) the two-week period starts on a Sunday and falls within the period` `the first day of the two-week period`)
    AND `s 153.8(2) the claim is made in time` `the day on which I make the claim`

-- s 153.9, with s 153.7(2) and (3). Whether the claimant is eligible for the benefit for the two-week period.
@export Am I eligible for the Emergency Response Benefit for this two-week period (s 153.9)?
GIVEN `I am a claimant of the kind described in paragraph 153.5(2)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Could a benefit period for Employment Insurance benefits have been established for you on or after March 15, 2020 for regular benefits or for most special benefits (a claimant under paragraph 153.5(2)(b))?
      `I am a claimant of the kind described in paragraph 153.5(2)(c) or (d)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you unable to start working for reasons related to COVID-19 after your Employment Insurance benefits ended, were all paid or reached a maximum (a claimant under paragraph 153.5(2)(c) or (d))?
      `I reside in Canada` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you reside in Canada?
      `my age in years` IS A NUMBER @desc How old are you, in years?
      `my insurable earnings in 2019` IS A NUMBER @desc What were your insurable earnings in 2019, in dollars?
      `my insurable earnings in the 52 weeks before I make the claim` IS A NUMBER @desc What were your insurable earnings in the 52 weeks before the day you make the claim, in dollars?
      `I stopped working` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you stop working, whether employed or self-employed?
      `I left my employment voluntarily` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you leave your employment voluntarily?
      `the greatest number of consecutive days in the two-week period on which I stopped working` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the greatest number of consecutive days within the two-week period on which you stopped working?
      `my income from employment or self-employment for those days` IS A NUMBER @desc What income from employment or self-employment did you have for those days, in dollars?
      `the greatest number of consecutive days in the two-week period with no income from employment or self-employment` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the greatest number of consecutive days within the two-week period for which you had no income from employment or self-employment?
      `my total income from employment and self-employment over the four weeks for which the benefit is paid` IS A NUMBER @desc What was your total income from employment and self-employment over the four weeks for which the benefit is paid, in dollars?
      `I receive another benefit under the Employment Insurance Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you receive a benefit under the Employment Insurance Act other than the Emergency Response Benefit?
      `I receive provincial allowances or benefits because of pregnancy` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you receive allowances, money or other benefits under a provincial plan because of pregnancy?
      `I receive provincial allowances or benefits because I am caring for a new-born or adopted child` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you receive allowances, money or other benefits under a provincial plan because you are caring for a new-born child or a child placed with you for adoption?
      `I receive an income support payment under the Canada Emergency Response Benefit Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you receive an income support payment under the Canada Emergency Response Benefit Act?
      `I receive a Canada emergency student benefit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you receive a Canada emergency student benefit under the Canada Emergency Student Benefit Act?
      `I received the Emergency Response Benefit for the week` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you receive the Emergency Response Benefit for the week in question?
      `I was not eligible for the week only because I received an income support payment under the Canada Emergency Response Benefit Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you not eligible for that week only because you received an income support payment under the Canada Emergency Response Benefit Act?
      `the Commission has informed the Minister that the Canada Emergency Response Benefit Act should not apply to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Commission informed the Minister, under subsection 15(2) of the Canada Emergency Response Benefit Act, that subsection 15(1) should not apply to you?
      `I was not eligible for the week only because I received a Canada emergency student benefit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you not eligible for that week only because you received a Canada emergency student benefit?
      `the Commission has informed the Minister that the Canada Emergency Student Benefit Act should not apply to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Commission informed the Minister, under subsection 15.1(2) of the Canada Emergency Student Benefit Act, that subsection 15.1(1) should not apply to you?
      `a benefit period established for me begins after I received the Emergency Response Benefit or an income support payment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does a benefit period established for you (including one under Part VIII) begin after you received the Emergency Response Benefit or an income support payment under the Canada Emergency Response Benefit Act?
      `I receive money or financial aid from my province for reasons related to COVID-19` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you receive a sum of money or financial aid from your province, under a provincial Act or any other provincial mechanism, for reasons related to COVID-19?
      `I receive financial aid under an agreement referred to in section 63` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you receive financial aid because you entered into an agreement referred to in section 63 of the Act?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I eligible for the Emergency Response Benefit for this two-week period` IF
        `s 153.7(2) the claimant remains eligible despite provincial money or financial aid` `eligible apart from the provincial aid` `I receive money or financial aid from my province for reasons related to COVID-19`
    AND `s 153.7(3) the claimant remains eligible despite financial aid under section 63` `eligible apart from the provincial aid` `I receive financial aid under an agreement referred to in section 63`
    WHERE
        `eligible apart from the provincial aid` MEANS
            `s 153.9 the claimant is eligible for the emergency response benefit` `the conditions of subsection (1) are met` `a ground of ineligibility applies`
        `the earnings test is met` MEANS
            `s 153.9(1)(a)(iii) insurable earnings of at least $5,000` `my insurable earnings in 2019` `my insurable earnings in the 52 weeks before I make the claim`
        `the income deeming applies` MEANS
            `s 153.9(4) the claimant is deemed to meet the requirements on ceasing work and on income` `my total income from employment and self-employment over the four weeks for which the benefit is paid`
        `the conditions of subsection (1) are met` MEANS
            `s 153.9(1) the claimant meets the conditions of eligibility` `paragraph (a)` `paragraph (b)` `paragraph (c)`
        `paragraph (a)` MEANS
            `s 153.9(1)(a) eligible as a claimant who ceases working`
                `I reside in Canada` `my age in years` `the earnings test is met`
                (`s 153.9(3) the claimant ceases working for the purpose of subsection (1)` `I stopped working` `I left my employment voluntarily`)
                `the greatest number of consecutive days in the two-week period on which I stopped working`
                `my income from employment or self-employment for those days`
                `the income deeming applies`
        `paragraph (b)` MEANS
            `s 153.9(1)(b) eligible as a claimant who could have had a benefit period established`
                `I am a claimant of the kind described in paragraph 153.5(2)(b)`
                `the greatest number of consecutive days in the two-week period with no income from employment or self-employment`
                `the income deeming applies`
        `paragraph (c)` MEANS
            `s 153.9(1)(c) eligible as a claimant who is unable to start working`
                `I am a claimant of the kind described in paragraph 153.5(2)(c) or (d)`
                `I reside in Canada` `my age in years` `the earnings test is met`
                `the greatest number of consecutive days in the two-week period with no income from employment or self-employment`
                `the income deeming applies`
        `a ground of ineligibility applies` MEANS
            `s 153.9(2) a ground of ineligibility applies to the claimant`
                `I receive another benefit under the Employment Insurance Act`
                `I receive provincial allowances or benefits because of pregnancy`
                `I receive provincial allowances or benefits because I am caring for a new-born or adopted child`
                `I receive an income support payment under the Canada Emergency Response Benefit Act`
                (`s 153.9(5) the claimant is deemed to have been eligible despite paragraph (2)(c)` `I received the Emergency Response Benefit for the week` `I was not eligible for the week only because I received an income support payment under the Canada Emergency Response Benefit Act` `the Commission has informed the Minister that the Canada Emergency Response Benefit Act should not apply to me`)
                `I receive a Canada emergency student benefit`
                (`s 153.9(6) the claimant is deemed to have been eligible despite paragraph (2)(d)` `I received the Emergency Response Benefit for the week` `I was not eligible for the week only because I received a Canada emergency student benefit` `the Commission has informed the Minister that the Canada Emergency Student Benefit Act should not apply to me`)
                `a benefit period established for me begins after I received the Emergency Response Benefit or an income support payment`

-- s 153.7(1) with s 153.8(1.1). The benefit is payable to a claimant who makes a claim and is eligible; for the week
-- beginning September 27, 2020 it is not payable unless it was paid or payable for an earlier week.
@export Is the Emergency Response Benefit payable to me for this week (ss 153.7(1), 153.8(1.1))?
GIVEN `I am a claimant for the benefit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a claimant for the Emergency Response Benefit?
      `I have made a claim under section 153.8` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you made a claim for the benefit?
      `I am eligible for the benefit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you eligible for the benefit for this week (see the question on eligibility)?
      `the Sunday that begins the week` IS A DATE @desc What is the Sunday that begins the week? (a date)
      `the benefit was paid or payable to me for a week beginning before September 27, 2020` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the benefit paid, or payable, to you for a week that began before September 27, 2020?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the Emergency Response Benefit payable to me for this week` IF
        `s 153.7(1) the emergency response benefit is payable to the claimant` `I am a claimant for the benefit` `I have made a claim under section 153.8` `I am eligible for the benefit`
    AND `s 153.8(1.1) the benefit is not barred for the week` `the Sunday that begins the week` `the benefit was paid or payable to me for a week beginning before September 27, 2020`

-- s 153.10. The weekly amount is $500, and provincial assistance does not reduce it; the family supplement of section 16
-- or subsections 152.17(1) to (4) applies to it.
@export How much Emergency Response Benefit do I get for a week, in dollars (s 153.10)?
GIVEN `I receive money or financial aid from my province for reasons related to COVID-19` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you receive a sum of money or financial aid from your province, under a provincial Act or any other provincial mechanism, for reasons related to COVID-19?
      `the increase to my rate for a family supplement` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the increase to your weekly rate under the family supplement of section 16 or subsections 152.17(1) to (4), in dollars? (0 if none)
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How much Emergency Response Benefit do I get for a week` IS
    `s 153.10 the amount of the emergency response benefit for a week, with the family supplement` `I receive money or financial aid from my province for reasons related to COVID-19` `the increase to my rate for a family supplement`

-- s 153.11. 28 weeks, less the weeks for which you receive a payment under the Canada Emergency Response Benefit Act or a
-- Canada emergency student benefit.
@export For how many weeks at most can I be paid the Emergency Response Benefit (s 153.11)?
GIVEN `the weeks for which I receive a Canada Emergency Response Benefit payment or a Canada emergency student benefit` IS A NUMBER @desc For how many weeks do you receive an income support payment under the Canada Emergency Response Benefit Act or a Canada emergency student benefit?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `For how many weeks at most can I be paid the Emergency Response Benefit` IS
    `s 153.11 the maximum number of weeks for which the emergency response benefit may be paid` `the weeks for which I receive a Canada Emergency Response Benefit payment or a Canada emergency student benefit`

@export Can the Emergency Response Benefit still be paid to me for another week (s 153.11)?
GIVEN `the weeks for which the benefit has already been paid to me` IS A NUMBER @desc For how many weeks has the Emergency Response Benefit already been paid to you?
      `the weeks for which I receive a Canada Emergency Response Benefit payment or a Canada emergency student benefit` IS A NUMBER @desc For how many weeks do you receive an income support payment under the Canada Emergency Response Benefit Act or a Canada emergency student benefit?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can the Emergency Response Benefit still be paid to me for another week` IS
    `s 153.11 the benefit may still be paid for another week` `the weeks for which the benefit has already been paid to me` `the weeks for which I receive a Canada Emergency Response Benefit payment or a Canada emergency student benefit`

-- s 153.8(3), (7). My duty to give the Minister information, and the Commission's duty to decide and tell me.
@export Must I give the Minister the information the Minister asks for about my claim (s 153.8(3))?
GIVEN `the Minister requires information in respect of my claim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Minister asked you for information about your claim for the Emergency Response Benefit?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I give the Minister the information the Minister asks for about my claim` IF
    `s 153.8(3) the claimant must provide the Minister with the information` `the Minister requires information in respect of my claim`

@export Must the Commission decide my claim for the Emergency Response Benefit and tell me its decision (s 153.8(7))?
GIVEN `the Commission has received my claim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Commission received your claim for the Emergency Response Benefit?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the Commission decide my claim for the Emergency Response Benefit and tell me its decision` IF
    `s 153.8(7) the Commission must decide whether the claimant is eligible and whether the benefit is payable, and notify the claimant` `the Commission has received my claim`

-- s 153.8(5), (6). No benefit period is to be established for a benefit of 153.5(3)(a) beginning March 15 to September 26,
-- 2020, nor September 27 to October 3 if the benefit was already paid and the maximum weeks has not been claimed.
@export Is a benefit period barred from being established for me beginning on this day (s 153.8(5), (6))?
GIVEN `the first day of the benefit period that would be established` IS A DATE @desc On what day would the benefit period begin? (a date)
      `the benefit is a regular benefit, a sickness benefit or another benefit referred to in paragraph 153.5(3)(a)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would the benefit be one of the benefits under section 152.03 or under Part I other than sections 22 to 24 (regular and sickness benefits)?
      `the Emergency Response Benefit was paid or payable to me for a week beginning before September 27, 2020` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the Emergency Response Benefit paid, or payable, to you for a week that began before September 27, 2020?
      `the number of weeks for which I have claimed the Emergency Response Benefit` IS A NUMBER @desc For how many weeks have you claimed the Emergency Response Benefit?
      `the weeks for which I receive a Canada Emergency Response Benefit payment or a Canada emergency student benefit` IS A NUMBER @desc For how many weeks do you receive an income support payment under the Canada Emergency Response Benefit Act or a Canada emergency student benefit?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
-- When s 153.11 gives no maximum (more than 28 weeks of CERB or CESB, fork F-ei6-6) the text does not say what
-- the bar of s 153.8(6) does; this question takes the maximum as 0, so the bar does not apply (assumed, not ruled).
DECIDE `Is a benefit period barred from being established for me beginning on this day` IF
    `s 153.8(5) and (6) no benefit period is to be established`
        `the first day of the benefit period that would be established`
        `the benefit is a regular benefit, a sickness benefit or another benefit referred to in paragraph 153.5(3)(a)`
        `the Emergency Response Benefit was paid or payable to me for a week beginning before September 27, 2020`
        `the number of weeks for which I have claimed the Emergency Response Benefit`
        `the maximum number of weeks`
    WHERE
        `the maximum number of weeks` MEANS
            CONSIDER `s 153.11 the maximum number of weeks for which the emergency response benefit may be paid` `the weeks for which I receive a Canada Emergency Response Benefit payment or a Canada emergency student benefit`
            WHEN JUST n THEN n
            WHEN NOTHING THEN 0

-- s 153.121. A benefit period established before March 15, 2020 ends the day before the first week for which the benefit is paid.
@export On what day does my earlier benefit period end because I was paid the Emergency Response Benefit (s 153.121)?
GIVEN `the first day of my benefit period` IS A DATE @desc On what day did your benefit period begin? (a date)
      `the Sunday that begins the first week for which I was paid the benefit` IS A DATE @desc What is the Sunday that begins the first week for which the Emergency Response Benefit was paid to you? (a date)
      `a decision after a reconsideration made it begin before March 15, 2020 after I was paid` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was a decision that gives you a benefit period beginning before March 15, 2020 made, after a reconsideration under section 112, after you had been paid the Emergency Response Benefit?
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `On what day does my earlier benefit period end because I was paid the Emergency Response Benefit` IS
    `s 153.121(1) the last day of the benefit period` `the first day of my benefit period` `the Sunday that begins the first week for which I was paid the benefit` `a decision after a reconsideration made it begin before March 15, 2020 after I was paid`

-- s 153.121(2). After such a reconsideration the benefit period does not end, and the benefit paid is treated as paid when
-- you were not eligible by reason of paragraph 153.9(2)(a) (you receive another benefit under the Act).
@export Does my benefit period stay open, and am I treated as not eligible for the Emergency Response Benefit, after a reconsideration (s 153.121(2))?
GIVEN `a decision after a reconsideration made it begin before March 15, 2020 after I was paid` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was a decision that gives you a benefit period beginning before March 15, 2020 made, after a reconsideration under section 112, after you had been paid the Emergency Response Benefit?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does my benefit period stay open, and am I treated as not eligible for the Emergency Response Benefit, after a reconsideration` IF
    `s 153.121(2) the benefit period does not end and the claimant is deemed not to have been eligible by reason of paragraph 153.9(2)(a)` `a decision after a reconsideration made it begin before March 15, 2020 after I was paid`

-- s 153.13. The weeks for which the benefit was paid are not taken into account in establishing a benefit period.
@export Is this week left out when my benefit period is established (s 153.13)?
GIVEN `the Sunday that begins the week` IS A DATE @desc What is the Sunday that begins the week? (a date)
      `the Emergency Response Benefit was paid to me for that week` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the Emergency Response Benefit paid to you for that week?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is this week left out when my benefit period is established` IF
    null (`s 153.13 the weeks taken into account in establishing the benefit period` (LIST `the Sunday that begins the week`) (IF `the Emergency Response Benefit was paid to me for that week` THEN LIST `the Sunday that begins the week` ELSE EMPTY))

-- s 153.12, s 153.1309 (section 138 as adapted): the Minister's use of the number, and my duty to have one.
@export May the Minister collect and use my Social Insurance Number for the Emergency Response Benefit (s 153.12)?
GIVEN `I make a claim under Part VIII.4` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you make a claim for the Emergency Response Benefit?
      `the purpose is the administration and enforcement of Part VIII.4` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the purpose the administration and enforcement of the Emergency Response Benefit?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the Minister collect and use my Social Insurance Number for the Emergency Response Benefit` IF
    `s 153.12 the Minister may collect and use the Social Insurance Number of the claimant` `I make a claim under Part VIII.4` `the purpose is the administration and enforcement of Part VIII.4`

@export Must I have a Social Insurance Number (s 153.1309, section 138 as adapted)?
GIVEN `the day on which the adapted provision is applied` IS A DATE @desc On what day do you want the answer for? (a date)
      `I am employed in insurable employment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you employed in insurable employment?
      `I am a self-employed person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a self-employed person?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I have a Social Insurance Number` IF
    `s 153.1309 as adapted s 138 the person must have a Social Insurance Number assigned under an Act of Parliament`
        (`s 153.14 the provision still applies on the day` `the day on which the adapted provision is applied` NOTHING)
        `I am employed in insurable employment` `I am a self-employed person`

-- s 153.1301 (section 44 as adapted): I must return a payment I was not eligible for, or the excess.
@export Must I return an Emergency Response Benefit payment without delay (s 153.1301)?
GIVEN `the day on which the adapted provision is applied` IS A DATE @desc On what day do you want the answer for? (a date)
      `I received or obtained a payment for which I was not eligible` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you receive or obtain an Emergency Response Benefit payment for which you were not eligible?
      `I received a payment above the amount for which I was eligible` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you receive an Emergency Response Benefit payment above the amount for which you were eligible?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I return an Emergency Response Benefit payment without delay` IF
    `s 153.1301 as adapted s 44 the person must return the amount without delay`
        (`s 153.14 the provision still applies on the day` `the day on which the adapted provision is applied` NOTHING)
        `I received or obtained a payment for which I was not eligible`
        `I received a payment above the amount for which I was eligible`

@export How much of an Emergency Response Benefit payment must I return, in dollars (s 153.1301)?
GIVEN `the day on which the adapted provision is applied` IS A DATE @desc On what day do you want the answer for? (a date)
      `I was eligible for the payment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you eligible for the Emergency Response Benefit payment you received?
      `the amount of the payment I received or obtained` IS A NUMBER @desc What was the amount of the payment you received or obtained, in dollars?
      `the amount for which I was eligible` IS A NUMBER @desc What was the amount for which you were eligible, in dollars? (0 if you were not eligible)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `How much of an Emergency Response Benefit payment must I return` IS
    `s 153.1301 as adapted s 44 the amount to be returned`
        (`s 153.14 the provision still applies on the day` `the day on which the adapted provision is applied` NOTHING)
        `I was eligible for the payment`
        `the amount of the payment I received or obtained`
        `the amount for which I was eligible`

-- s 153.1302 (section 50 as adapted).
@export Am I not eligible for the Emergency Response Benefit until I give the information or attend as required (s 153.1302)?
GIVEN `the day on which the adapted provision is applied` IS A DATE @desc On what day do you want the answer for? (a date)
      `I have provided the Minister with the information required for my claim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you provided the Minister with the information required in respect of your claim?
      `the Commission requires me to be at a suitable place at a suitable time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the Commission require you to be at a suitable place at a suitable time to make your claim in person, or to give more information about it?
      `I have complied with that requirement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you complied with that requirement?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I not eligible for the Emergency Response Benefit until I give the information or attend as required` IF
    `s 153.1302 as adapted s 50(1) the claimant is not eligible until they provide the information or comply`
        (`s 153.14 the provision still applies on the day` `the day on which the adapted provision is applied` NOTHING)
        `I have provided the Minister with the information required for my claim`
        `the Commission requires me to be at a suitable place at a suitable time`
        `I have complied with that requirement`

@export May the Commission require me to attend in person or give more information about my Emergency Response Benefit claim (s 153.1302)?
GIVEN `the day on which the adapted provision is applied` IS A DATE @desc On what day do you want the answer for? (a date)
      `my claim concerns the Emergency Response Benefit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your claim, or the information asked for, about the Emergency Response Benefit?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the Commission require me to attend in person or give more information about my Emergency Response Benefit claim` IF
    `s 153.1302 as adapted s 50(2) the Commission may require the claimant to be at a suitable place at a suitable time`
        (`s 153.14 the provision still applies on the day` `the day on which the adapted provision is applied` NOTHING)
        `my claim concerns the Emergency Response Benefit`

-- s 153.1303 (section 52 as adapted).
@export Must the Commission calculate the amount and tell me its decision (s 153.1303)?
GIVEN `the day on which the adapted provision is applied` IS A DATE @desc On what day do you want the answer for? (a date)
      `the Commission decides that I received money for which I was not eligible` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Commission decided that you received Emergency Response Benefit money for which you were not eligible?
      `the Commission decides that I did not receive money for which I was eligible` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Commission decided that you did not receive Emergency Response Benefit money for which you were eligible?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the Commission calculate the amount and tell me its decision` IF
    `s 153.1303 as adapted s 52(2) the Commission must calculate the amount and notify the claimant of its decision`
        (`s 153.14 the provision still applies on the day` `the day on which the adapted provision is applied` NOTHING)
        `the Commission decides that I received money for which I was not eligible`
        `the Commission decides that I did not receive money for which I was eligible`

@export How much is payable to me because I was eligible but was not paid (s 153.1303, section 52(4) as adapted)?
GIVEN `the day on which the adapted provision is applied` IS A DATE @desc On what day do you want the answer for? (a date)
      `the Commission decides that I was eligible to receive money` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Commission decided that you were eligible to receive Emergency Response Benefit money?
      `the money was not paid to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the money not paid to you?
      `the amount the Commission calculated` IS A NUMBER @desc What amount did the Commission calculate, in dollars?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `How much is payable to me because I was eligible but was not paid` IS
    `s 153.1303 as adapted s 52(4) the amount payable to the claimant`
        (`s 153.14 the provision still applies on the day` `the day on which the adapted provision is applied` NOTHING)
        `the Commission decides that I was eligible to receive money`
        `the money was not paid to me`
        `the amount the Commission calculated`

-- s 153.1305 (section 112 as adapted): asking the Commission to reconsider.
@export May I ask the Commission to reconsider its decision now (s 153.1305(1))?
GIVEN `the day on which the adapted provision is applied` IS A DATE @desc On what day do you want the answer for? (a date)
      `I am the claimant or another person who is the subject of the decision, or the claimant's employer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you the claimant or another person who is the subject of the decision, or the employer of the claimant?
      `the day on which the decision was communicated to me` IS A DATE @desc On what day was the decision communicated to you? (a date)
      `the day on which I make the request` IS A DATE @desc On what day do you make the request? (a date)
      `the Commission has allowed me further time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Commission allowed you any further time to make the request?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I ask the Commission to reconsider its decision now` IF
    `s 153.1305(1) as adapted s 112(1) the person may make a request for reconsideration`
        (`s 153.14 the provision still applies on the day` `the day on which the adapted provision is applied` NOTHING)
        `I am the claimant or another person who is the subject of the decision, or the claimant's employer`
        `the day on which the decision was communicated to me`
        `the day on which I make the request`
        `the Commission has allowed me further time`

@export Is my request for reconsideration in the form required (s 153.1305(2), section 112(4) as added)?
GIVEN `the day on which the adapted provision is applied` IS A DATE @desc On what day do you want the answer for? (a date)
      `my request is in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your request in writing?
      `my request gives my name and my social insurance number or business number` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your request give your name and your social insurance number or the business number assigned to you by the Minister of National Revenue?
      `my request gives my address and telephone number` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your request give your address and telephone number?
      `my request gives my facsimile number and email address, if I have any` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your request give your facsimile number and email address, if you have any?
      `my request gives the date on which the decision was communicated to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your request give the date on which the decision was communicated to you?
      `my request gives my reasons` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your request give the reasons why you are requesting a reconsideration?
      `my request gives any relevant information not previously provided` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your request give any relevant information that you did not previously provide to the Commission?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my request for reconsideration in the form required` IF
    `s 153.1305(2) as added s 112(4) the request for reconsideration is in the form required`
        (`s 153.14 the provision still applies on the day` `the day on which the adapted provision is applied` NOTHING)
        `my request is in writing`
        `my request gives my name and my social insurance number or business number`
        `my request gives my address and telephone number`
        `my request gives my facsimile number and email address, if I have any`
        `my request gives the date on which the decision was communicated to me`
        `my request gives my reasons`
        `my request gives any relevant information not previously provided`

@export Have I filed my request for reconsideration as required (s 153.1305(2), section 112(5) as added)?
GIVEN `the day on which the adapted provision is applied` IS A DATE @desc On what day do you want the answer for? (a date)
      `I filed it at the address, facsimile number or email address the Commission provides on the website of the Department of Employment and Social Development` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you file the request with the Commission at the address, facsimile number or email address provided on the website of the Department of Employment and Social Development?
      `I filed it by the electronic filing procedure the Commission provides on that website` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you file it in accordance with the electronic filing procedure provided on that website?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Have I filed my request for reconsideration as required` IF
    `s 153.1305(2) as added s 112(5) the request for reconsideration is filed as required`
        (`s 153.14 the provision still applies on the day` `the day on which the adapted provision is applied` NOTHING)
        `I filed it at the address, facsimile number or email address the Commission provides on the website of the Department of Employment and Social Development`
        `I filed it by the electronic filing procedure the Commission provides on that website`

-- s 153.1306 (write-off), s 153.1307 (no review), s 153.1308 (certificate and judgment).
@export May the Commission write off the amount I owe under section 43 (s 153.1306(1))?
GIVEN `the day on which the adapted provision is applied` IS A DATE @desc On what day do you want the answer for? (a date)
      `the amount I owe under section 43` IS A NUMBER @desc How much do you owe under section 43, in dollars?
      `the debtor is deceased` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the debtor deceased?
      `the debtor is a discharged bankrupt` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the debtor a discharged bankrupt?
      `the debtor is an undischarged bankrupt whose trustee has been discharged and the final dividend paid` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the debtor an undischarged bankrupt in respect of whom the final dividend has been paid and the trustee has been discharged?
      `the overpayment arose from an error made by the debtor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the overpayment arise from an error made by the debtor?
      `the overpayment arose from a false or misleading declaration or representation made by the debtor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the overpayment arise from a false or misleading declaration or representation made by the debtor, whether or not the debtor knew it to be false or misleading?
      `the overpayment arose from a retrospective decision or ruling made under Part IV` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the overpayment arise from a retrospective decision or ruling made under Part IV of the Act?
      `the overpayment arose from the Commission providing a weekly amount above $500` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the overpayment arise from the Commission providing a weekly Emergency Response Benefit amount above $500?
      `the Commission considers the amount uncollectable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the Commission consider, having regard to all the circumstances, that the amount is uncollectable?
      `the Commission considers repayment would cause the debtor undue hardship` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the Commission consider that repaying the amount would cause the debtor undue hardship?
      `the Commission considers the cost of collecting would likely equal or exceed the amount` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the Commission consider that the administrative costs of collecting the amount would likely equal or exceed it?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the Commission write off the amount I owe under section 43` IF
    `s 153.1306(1) the Commission may write off the amount payable under section 43`
        (`s 153.14 the provision still applies on the day` `the day on which the adapted provision is applied` NOTHING)
        `the amount I owe under section 43`
        `the debtor is deceased`
        `the debtor is a discharged bankrupt`
        `the debtor is an undischarged bankrupt whose trustee has been discharged and the final dividend paid`
        (`s 153.1306(1)(e) the overpayment does not arise from the debtor's error or declaration but from a retrospective ruling or an excess weekly amount`
            `the overpayment arose from an error made by the debtor`
            `the overpayment arose from a false or misleading declaration or representation made by the debtor`
            `the overpayment arose from a retrospective decision or ruling made under Part IV`
            `the overpayment arose from the Commission providing a weekly amount above $500`)
        (`s 153.1306(1)(f) the Commission considers that the amount is uncollectable or that collecting it would be unduly hard or costly`
            `the Commission considers the amount uncollectable`
            `the Commission considers repayment would cause the debtor undue hardship`
            `the Commission considers the cost of collecting would likely equal or exceed the amount`)

@export May the Commission write off the part of the amount I owe under section 47 that I received before it told me of the overpayment (s 153.1306(2))?
GIVEN `the day on which the adapted provision is applied` IS A DATE @desc On what day do you want the answer for? (a date)
      `the overpayment arose from an error made by the debtor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the overpayment arise from an error made by the debtor?
      `the overpayment arose from a false or misleading declaration or representation made by the debtor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the overpayment arise from a false or misleading declaration or representation made by the debtor, whether or not the debtor knew it to be false or misleading?
      `the overpayment arose from a delay or error made by the Commission in processing the claim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the overpayment arise from a delay or error made by the Commission in processing a claim for the Emergency Response Benefit?
      `the overpayment arose from retrospective control procedures or a retrospective review` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the overpayment arise from retrospective control procedures or a retrospective review initiated by the Commission?
      `the overpayment arose from an error made on the record of employment by the employer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the overpayment arise from an error made by the employer on the record of employment?
      `the overpayment arose from an incorrect calculation by the employer of the debtor's insurable earnings` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the overpayment arise from an incorrect calculation by the employer of the debtor's insurable earnings?
      `the overpayment arose from an error in insuring the debtor's employment or other activity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the overpayment arise from an error in insuring the debtor's employment or other activity?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the Commission write off the part of the amount I owe under section 47 that I received before it told me of the overpayment` IF
    `s 153.1306(2) the Commission may write off the portion of the amount owing under section 47 received before notification`
        (`s 153.14 the provision still applies on the day` `the day on which the adapted provision is applied` NOTHING)
        `the overpayment arose from an error made by the debtor`
        `the overpayment arose from a false or misleading declaration or representation made by the debtor`
        `the overpayment arose from a delay or error made by the Commission in processing the claim`
        `the overpayment arose from retrospective control procedures or a retrospective review`
        `the overpayment arose from an error made on the record of employment by the employer`
        `the overpayment arose from an incorrect calculation by the employer of the debtor's insurable earnings`
        `the overpayment arose from an error in insuring the debtor's employment or other activity`

@export Is the Commission's decision about a write-off closed to reconsideration (s 153.1307)?
GIVEN `the day on which the adapted provision is applied` IS A DATE @desc On what day do you want the answer for? (a date)
      `the decision is a decision of the Commission under section 153.1306` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the decision a decision of the Commission about writing off an amount, under section 153.1306?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the Commission's decision about a write-off closed to reconsideration` IF
    `s 153.1307 as adapted s 112.1 the decision is not subject to review under section 112`
        (`s 153.14 the provision still applies on the day` `the day on which the adapted provision is applied` NOTHING)
        `the decision is a decision of the Commission under section 153.1306`

@export May the Commission certify the amount I have not paid (s 153.1308)?
GIVEN `the day on which the adapted provision is applied` IS A DATE @desc On what day do you want the answer for? (a date)
      `the Part under which the amount is payable` IS A `Part of the Act` @desc Under which Part of the Act is the amount payable? (Part I, II, VII.1 or VIII.4 are the ones that count)
      `the amount has not been paid` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the amount not been paid?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the Commission certify the amount I have not paid` IF
    `s 153.1308 as adapted s 126(1) the Commission may certify the unpaid amount`
        (`s 153.14 the provision still applies on the day` `the day on which the adapted provision is applied` NOTHING)
        `the Part under which the amount is payable`
        `the amount has not been paid`

@export Does a certificate registered in the Federal Court have the force of a judgment against me (s 153.1308)?
GIVEN `the day on which the adapted provision is applied` IS A DATE @desc On what day do you want the answer for? (a date)
      `the certificate has been produced to the Federal Court and registered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the certificate been produced to the Federal Court and registered there?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does a certificate registered in the Federal Court have the force of a judgment against me` IF
    `s 153.1308 as adapted s 126(2) the certificate has the force and effect of a judgment of the Federal Court for a debt of the amount specified`
        (`s 153.14 the provision still applies on the day` `the day on which the adapted provision is applied` NOTHING)
        `the certificate has been produced to the Federal Court and registered`

-- s 153.1310. Special rules for a person who was already claiming regular or sickness benefits when the benefit began.
@export Do the special rules for people already claiming benefits apply to me (s 153.1310)?
GIVEN `I made an initial claim for regular or sickness benefits` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you make an initial claim for benefits under section 152.03 or under Part I other than sections 22 to 24 (regular or sickness benefits)?
      `I had a benefit period established on or after March 15, 2020 before the Part came into force` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you have a benefit period established, on or after March 15, 2020, before Part VIII.4 came into force retroactively?
      `I would have had one but for the Part coming into force on March 15, 2020` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would you have had a benefit period established on or after March 15, 2020 for those benefits but for Part VIII.4 coming into force on that day?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do the special rules for people already claiming benefits apply to me` IF
    `s 153.1310 the special rules apply to the person`
        `I made an initial claim for regular or sickness benefits`
        `I had a benefit period established on or after March 15, 2020 before the Part came into force`
        `I would have had one but for the Part coming into force on March 15, 2020`

@export How much Emergency Response Benefit am I paid for a week in which I received regular or sickness benefits, in dollars (s 153.1310(c))?
GIVEN `the special rules apply to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the special rules for people already claiming benefits apply to you?
      `the regular or sickness benefits I received for the week` IS A NUMBER @desc How much did you receive in regular or sickness benefits for the week, in dollars?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `How much Emergency Response Benefit am I paid for a week in which I received regular or sickness benefits` IS
    `s 153.1310(c)(i) the amount of the emergency response benefit to be paid for the week` `the special rules apply to me` `the regular or sickness benefits I received for the week`

@export How much of the benefits I received for the week is outside the duty to repay under section 44, in dollars (s 153.1310(c)(ii))?
GIVEN `the special rules apply to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the special rules for people already claiming benefits apply to you?
      `the regular or sickness benefits I received for the week` IS A NUMBER @desc How much did you receive in regular or sickness benefits for the week, in dollars?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `How much of the benefits I received for the week is outside section 44` IS
    `s 153.1310(c)(ii) the amount of benefits received for the week to which section 44 does not apply` `the special rules apply to me` `the regular or sickness benefits I received for the week`

@export Am I deemed to have made a claim for the Emergency Response Benefit (s 153.1310(a))?
GIVEN `the special rules apply to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the special rules for people already claiming benefits apply to you?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I deemed to have made a claim for the Emergency Response Benefit` IF
    `s 153.1310(a) the person is deemed to have made a claim for the emergency response benefit under section 153.8` `the special rules apply to me`

@export Must I still make my claim in the way subsection 153.8(1) requires (s 153.1310(b))?
GIVEN `the special rules apply to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the special rules for people already claiming benefits apply to you?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I still make my claim in the way subsection 153.8(1) requires` IF
    `s 153.1310(b) the person must make the claim in accordance with subsection 153.8(1)` `the special rules apply to me`

-- s 153.14. Whether the Part still applies on a day.
@export Does a provision added to Part VIII.4 by an Interim Order still apply on this day (s 153.14)?
GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE @desc On what day do you want the answer for? (a date)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does a provision added to Part VIII.4 by an Interim Order still apply on this day` IF
    `s 153.14 the provision still applies on the day` `the day` NOTHING

§ `Part VIII.5 - temporary measures to facilitate access to benefits (September 27, 2020 to September 25, 2021)`

-- The group applies only if your claim or benefit period falls in 2020 or 2021: ask "Did this happen to you?" first.
-- Each question asks for the day the provision is applied to (usually the day of the initial claim, or the day the benefit
-- period begins), and checks that Part VIII.5 had not ceased to apply on it (s 153.196).

-- The BOOLEAN that most Part VIII.5 rules take, for the provisions that fall under subsection 153.196(1).
GIVEN day IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `ei6 seat Part VIII.5 has not ceased to apply on the day` IF
    `s 153.196 the provision applies on the day` `ei6 any other provision of Part VIII.5` day NOTHING

GIVEN day IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `ei6 seat sections 153.1922 to 153.1924 have not ceased to apply on the day` IF
    `s 153.196 the provision applies on the day` `ei6 sections 153.1922 to 153.1924` day NOTHING

GIVEN day IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `ei6 seat section 153.19 has not ceased to apply on the day` IF
    `s 153.196 the provision applies on the day` `ei6 section 153.19` day NOTHING

-- s 153.196. Whether a provision of Part VIII.5 still applies on a day.
@export Does a provision of Part VIII.5 still apply on this day (s 153.196)?
GIVEN `the provision` IS A `ei6 Group of provisions of Part VIII.5 for cessation` @desc Which provision? Section 153.19, one of sections 153.1922 to 153.1924, or any other provision of Part VIII.5
      `the day` IS A DATE @desc On what day do you want the answer for? (a date)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does a provision of Part VIII.5 still apply on this day` IF
    `s 153.196 the provision applies on the day` `the provision` `the day` NOTHING

-- s 153.16. The regional rate of unemployment of 13.1%.
@export What regional rate of unemployment applies to me, in per cent (s 153.16)?
GIVEN `the day on which my interruption of earnings occurs` IS A DATE @desc On what day did your interruption of earnings occur? (a date)
      `the day on which I make my initial claim for benefits` IS A DATE @desc On what day do you make your initial claim for benefits? (a date)
      `the regional rate of unemployment that would otherwise apply to me, in per cent` IS A NUMBER @desc What regional rate of unemployment would otherwise apply to you, in per cent? (7.5 for 7.5%)
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What regional rate of unemployment applies to me, in per cent` IS
    100 TIMES `the rate that applies`
    WHERE
        `the later week begins` MEANS
            `s 153.16 the Sunday that begins the later of the weeks referred to in subsection 10(1)` `the day on which my interruption of earnings occurs` `the day on which I make my initial claim for benefits`
        `the rate that applies` MEANS
            `s 153.16 the regional rate of unemployment that applies to the claimant`
                (`ei6 seat Part VIII.5 has not ceased to apply on the day` `the later week begins`)
                `the day on which my interruption of earnings occurs`
                `the day on which I make my initial claim for benefits`
                (`the regional rate of unemployment that would otherwise apply to me, in per cent` DIVIDED BY 100)

-- s 153.161. Availability while attending a course not referred to.
@export Am I not entitled to be paid for a working day because I cannot prove I was available while attending a course (s 153.161(1))?
GIVEN `the day on which I make my initial claim for benefits` IS A DATE @desc On what day do you make your initial claim for benefits? (a date)
      `I attend a course, program of instruction or training to which I was not referred under paragraph 25(1)(a) or (b)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you attend a course, program of instruction or training to which you were not referred under paragraph 25(1)(a) or (b) of the Act?
      `I am unable to prove I was capable of and available for work on that day` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you unable to prove that on that working day you were capable of and available for work?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I not entitled to be paid for a working day because I cannot prove I was available while attending a course` IF
    `s 153.161(1) the claimant is not entitled to be paid benefits for the working day`
        (`ei6 seat Part VIII.5 has not ceased to apply on the day` `the day on which I make my initial claim for benefits`)
        `I attend a course, program of instruction or training to which I was not referred under paragraph 25(1)(a) or (b)`
        `I am unable to prove I was capable of and available for work on that day`

@export May the Commission, after paying me, require proof that I was available for work (s 153.161(2))?
GIVEN `the day on which I make my initial claim for benefits` IS A DATE @desc On what day do you make your initial claim for benefits? (a date)
      `benefits have been paid to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have benefits been paid to you?
      `I attended a course, program of instruction or training to which I was not referred under paragraph 25(1)(a) or (b)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you attend a course, program of instruction or training to which you were not referred under paragraph 25(1)(a) or (b) of the Act?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the Commission, after paying me, require proof that I was available for work` IF
    `s 153.161(2) the Commission may require proof that the claimant was capable of and available for work`
        (`ei6 seat Part VIII.5 has not ceased to apply on the day` `the day on which I make my initial claim for benefits`)
        `benefits have been paid to me`
        `I attended a course, program of instruction or training to which I was not referred under paragraph 25(1)(a) or (b)`

-- ss 153.17 to 153.172. Additional hours of insurable employment.
@export How many additional hours of insurable employment am I deemed to have (s 153.17)?
GIVEN `the day on which I make my initial claim for benefits` IS A DATE @desc On what day do you make your initial claim for benefits? (a date)
      `the day on which my interruption of earnings occurs` IS A DATE @desc On what day did your interruption of earnings occur? (a date)
      `my initial claim is for benefits under Part I` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your initial claim for benefits under Part I of the Act?
      `my claim is for benefits referred to in any of sections 21 to 23.3` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your claim for sickness, maternity, parental, compassionate care or family caregiver benefits (sections 21 to 23.3)?
      `my insurable hours were already increased under section 153.17` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have the insurable hours in your qualifying period already been increased under section 153.17 (or as it read on September 26, 2020)?
      `a benefit period was established in relation to that qualifying period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was a benefit period established in relation to that qualifying period?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `How many additional hours of insurable employment am I deemed to have` IS
    `s 153.17 the additional hours of insurable employment the claimant is deemed to have in the qualifying period`
        (`ei6 seat Part VIII.5 has not ceased to apply on the day` `the day on which I make my initial claim for benefits`)
        `my initial claim is for benefits under Part I`
        `the day on which I make my initial claim for benefits`
        `the day on which my interruption of earnings occurs`
        `my claim is for benefits referred to in any of sections 21 to 23.3`
        `my insurable hours were already increased under section 153.17`
        `a benefit period was established in relation to that qualifying period`

@export May I claim sickness, maternity, parental or caring benefits although I am not a major attachment claimant (s 153.171)?
GIVEN `the day on which I make my initial claim for benefits` IS A DATE @desc On what day do you make your initial claim for benefits? (a date)
      `I qualify to receive benefits under section 7` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you qualify to receive benefits under section 7?
      `I received the additional 300 hours of insurable employment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you receive the additional 300 hours of insurable employment under paragraph 153.17(1)(b)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I claim sickness, maternity, parental or caring benefits although I am not a major attachment claimant` IF
    `s 153.171 the claimant may make a claim for benefits under sections 21 to 23.3 although not a major attachment claimant`
        (`ei6 seat Part VIII.5 has not ceased to apply on the day` `the day on which I make my initial claim for benefits`)
        `I qualify to receive benefits under section 7`
        `I received the additional 300 hours of insurable employment`

@export May I ask for benefits under the Fishing Regulations rather than under section 7 (s 153.172)?
GIVEN `the day on which I make my initial claim for benefits` IS A DATE @desc On what day do you make your initial claim for benefits? (a date)
      `a benefit period could have been established for me under section 8 of the Fishing Regulations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Before section 153.17 came into force, could a benefit period have been established for you under section 8 of the Employment Insurance (Fishing) Regulations?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I ask for benefits under the Fishing Regulations rather than under section 7` IF
    `s 153.172 the claimant may make a request under section 112 to receive benefits under the Fishing Regulations rather than under section 7`
        (`ei6 seat Part VIII.5 has not ceased to apply on the day` `the day on which I make my initial claim for benefits`)
        `a benefit period could have been established for me under section 8 of the Fishing Regulations`

-- s 153.18. The qualifying period is extended by 28 weeks.
@export By how many weeks is my qualifying period extended (s 153.18)?
GIVEN `the day on which I make my initial claim for benefits` IS A DATE @desc On what day do you make your initial claim for benefits? (a date)
      `the day on which my interruption of earnings occurs` IS A DATE @desc On what day did your interruption of earnings occur? (a date)
      `I received the Emergency Response Benefit or an income support payment during my qualifying period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc During the 52-week qualifying period before your benefit period, did you receive the Emergency Response Benefit or an income support payment under the Canada Emergency Response Benefit Act?
      `my qualifying period was already extended` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a qualifying period of yours already been extended under section 153.18 (or as it read on August 29, 2020 or September 26, 2020)?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `By how many weeks is my qualifying period extended` IS
    `s 153.18 the number of weeks by which the qualifying period is extended`
        (`ei6 seat Part VIII.5 has not ceased to apply on the day` `the day on which I make my initial claim for benefits`)
        `the day on which I make my initial claim for benefits`
        `the day on which my interruption of earnings occurs`
        `I received the Emergency Response Benefit or an income support payment during my qualifying period`
        `my qualifying period was already extended`

@export On what day does my extended qualifying period begin (s 153.18)?
GIVEN `the day on which I make my initial claim for benefits` IS A DATE @desc On what day do you make your initial claim for benefits? (a date)
      `the day on which my interruption of earnings occurs` IS A DATE @desc On what day did your interruption of earnings occur? (a date)
      `I received the Emergency Response Benefit or an income support payment during my qualifying period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc During the 52-week qualifying period before your benefit period, did you receive the Emergency Response Benefit or an income support payment under the Canada Emergency Response Benefit Act?
      `my qualifying period was already extended` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a qualifying period of yours already been extended under section 153.18 (or as it read on August 29, 2020 or September 26, 2020)?
      `the first day of my qualifying period` IS A DATE @desc What is the first day of your qualifying period, before any extension? (a date)
      `the last day of my qualifying period` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day of your qualifying period? (a date)
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `On what day does my extended qualifying period begin` IS
    (`s 153.18 the qualifying period as extended` `the weeks of the extension` (`Period of days` OF `the first day of my qualifying period`, `the last day of my qualifying period`))'s `first day of the period`
    WHERE
        `the weeks of the extension` MEANS
            `s 153.18 the number of weeks by which the qualifying period is extended`
                (`ei6 seat Part VIII.5 has not ceased to apply on the day` `the day on which I make my initial claim for benefits`)
                `the day on which I make my initial claim for benefits`
                `the day on which my interruption of earnings occurs`
                `I received the Emergency Response Benefit or an income support payment during my qualifying period`
                `my qualifying period was already extended`

-- s 153.19. Late claims.
@export Is the loss of qualification from the changed hours good cause for my delay in claiming (s 153.19)?
GIVEN `the day on which I make my late claim` IS A DATE @desc On what day do you make your claim? (a date)
      `but for sections 153.17 and 153.18 as they read on August 29, 2020, I would not have qualified for benefits referred to in any of sections 22 to 24` IS A BOOLEAN @desc But for sections 153.17 and 153.18 as they read on August 29, 2020, would you not have qualified for maternity, parental, caring or work-sharing benefits (sections 22 to 24)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the loss of qualification from the changed hours good cause for my delay in claiming` IF
    `s 153.19 the fact is good cause for a delay in making a claim for the benefits`
        (`ei6 seat section 153.19 has not ceased to apply on the day` `the day on which I make my late claim`)
        `but for sections 153.17 and 153.18 as they read on August 29, 2020, I would not have qualified for benefits referred to in any of sections 22 to 24`

-- ss 153.191 to 153.1921. Waiting period, weekly insurable earnings, medical certificate.
@export Am I excused from serving a waiting period (s 153.191(1), (1.1))?
GIVEN `the Part under which I claim` IS A `Part of the Act` @desc Under which Part of the Act do you claim benefits? (Part I, VII.1 or VIII)
      `the first day of my benefit period` IS A DATE @desc On what day does your benefit period begin? (a date)
      `I receive benefits under section 21 or 152.03` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you receive sickness benefits under section 21 (employees) or section 152.03 (self-employed persons)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I excused from serving a waiting period` IF
        `s 153.191(1) the claimant need not serve a waiting period`
            (`ei6 seat Part VIII.5 has not ceased to apply on the day` `the first day of my benefit period`)
            `the Part under which I claim` `the first day of my benefit period`
    OR `s 153.191(1.1) the claimant need not serve a waiting period`
            (`ei6 seat Part VIII.5 has not ceased to apply on the day` `the first day of my benefit period`)
            `I receive benefits under section 21 or 152.03`

@export May I serve the waiting period although I need not (s 153.191(2))?
GIVEN `I need not serve a waiting period under subsection (1) or (1.1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you excused from serving a waiting period (see the question on waiting periods)?
      `I am entitled to a payment referred to in subsection 37(1) or 38(1) of the Regulations during that period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc During the waiting period, are you entitled to receive a payment referred to in subsection 37(1) or 38(1) of the Employment Insurance Regulations?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I serve the waiting period although I need not` IF
    `s 153.191(2) the claimant may nonetheless serve the waiting period` `I need not serve a waiting period under subsection (1) or (1.1)` `I am entitled to a payment referred to in subsection 37(1) or 38(1) of the Regulations during that period`

@export Do subsections 40(6) and 40.1(2) of the Regulations apply to my waiting period (s 153.191(3))?
GIVEN `my waiting period is one to which subsection (1) applies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your waiting period one that section 153.191(1) says you need not serve?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do subsections 40(6) and 40.1(2) of the Regulations apply to my waiting period` IF
    `s 153.191(3) subsections 40(6) and 40.1(2) of the Regulations apply to the waiting period` `my waiting period is one to which subsection (1) applies`

@export What weekly insurable earnings are used for me, in dollars (s 153.192(1))?
GIVEN `the first day of my benefit period` IS A DATE @desc On what day does your benefit period begin? (a date)
      `my insurable earnings in the calculation period` IS A NUMBER @desc What were your insurable earnings in the calculation period of subsection 14(4), in dollars?
      `the number of weeks in that period in which I had insurable earnings` IS A NUMBER @desc In how many weeks of that period did you have insurable earnings?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `What weekly insurable earnings are used for me` IS
    `s 153.192(1) the weekly insurable earnings of the claimant are deemed to be`
        (`ei6 seat Part VIII.5 has not ceased to apply on the day` `the first day of my benefit period`)
        `the first day of my benefit period`
        `my insurable earnings in the calculation period`
        `the number of weeks in that period in which I had insurable earnings`

@export What weekly insurable earnings are used for me as a self-employed person, in dollars (s 153.192(2))?
GIVEN `the first day of my benefit period` IS A DATE @desc On what day does your benefit period begin? (a date)
      `the aggregate of my amounts under paragraphs 152.16(1)(a) and (b)` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the aggregate of the amounts referred to in paragraphs 152.16(1)(a) and (b), in dollars?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `What weekly insurable earnings are used for me as a self-employed person` IS
    `s 153.192(2) the result of dividing the aggregate by 52, for a self-employed person`
        (`ei6 seat Part VIII.5 has not ceased to apply on the day` `the first day of my benefit period`)
        `the first day of my benefit period`
        `the aggregate of my amounts under paragraphs 152.16(1)(a) and (b)`

@export What weekly insurable earnings are used for me as a fisher, in dollars (s 153.192(3))?
GIVEN `the first day of my benefit period` IS A DATE @desc On what day does your benefit period begin? (a date)
      `my weekly insurable earnings under paragraph 8.1(a) of the Fishing Regulations` IS A NUMBER @desc What are your weekly insurable earnings under paragraph 8.1(a) of the Employment Insurance (Fishing) Regulations, in dollars?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `What weekly insurable earnings are used for me as a fisher` IS
    `s 153.192(3) the weekly insurable earnings of the fisher are deemed to be`
        (`ei6 seat Part VIII.5 has not ceased to apply on the day` `the first day of my benefit period`)
        `the first day of my benefit period`
        `my weekly insurable earnings under paragraph 8.1(a) of the Fishing Regulations`

@export Is the requirement to provide a medical certificate suspended for me (s 153.1921(1))?
GIVEN `the day on which I make my initial claim for benefits` IS A DATE @desc On what day do you make your initial claim for benefits? (a date)
      `the Commission has indicated otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Commission indicated that you must provide a medical certificate?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the requirement to provide a medical certificate suspended for me` IF
    `s 153.1921(1) the requirement to provide a medical certificate under subsection 40(1) of the Regulations is suspended`
        (`ei6 seat Part VIII.5 has not ceased to apply on the day` `the day on which I make my initial claim for benefits`)
        `the Commission has indicated otherwise`

@export May the Commission suspend the requirement of a medical certificate for my caring or self-employed sickness claim (s 153.1921(2))?
GIVEN `the day on which I make my initial claim for benefits` IS A DATE @desc On what day do you make your initial claim for benefits? (a date)
      `my claim is under one of sections 23.1, 23.2, 23.3 and 152.06 to 152.062` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your claim for compassionate care or family caregiver benefits (sections 23.1 to 23.3), or the self-employed equivalents (sections 152.06 to 152.062)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the Commission suspend the requirement of a medical certificate for my caring or self-employed sickness claim` IF
    `s 153.1921(2) the Commission may suspend the requirement to provide a medical certificate`
        (`ei6 seat Part VIII.5 has not ceased to apply on the day` `the day on which I make my initial claim for benefits`)
        `my claim is under one of sections 23.1, 23.2, 23.3 and 152.06 to 152.062`

-- ss 153.1922 to 153.1925. Fishers.
@export May I receive section 8.1 benefits under the Fishing Regulations by virtue of section 153.1922?
GIVEN `the day on which I make my initial claim for benefits` IS A DATE @desc On what day do you make your initial claim for benefits? (a date)
      `I meet the conditions under paragraph 8(2)(b) or (7)(b) of the Fishing Regulations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you meet the conditions under paragraph 8(2)(b) or (7)(b) of the Employment Insurance (Fishing) Regulations?
      `a day on which I received benefits under section 8.1 of the Fishing Regulations` IS A DATE @desc On what day did you receive benefits under section 8.1 of those Regulations? (a date; any one such day)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I receive section 8.1 benefits under the Fishing Regulations by virtue of section 153.1922` IF
    `s 153.1922 the fisher may receive benefits under section 8.1 of the Fishing Regulations by virtue of this section`
        (`ei6 seat sections 153.1922 to 153.1924 have not ceased to apply on the day` `the day on which I make my initial claim for benefits`)
        `I meet the conditions under paragraph 8(2)(b) or (7)(b) of the Fishing Regulations`
        `a day on which I received benefits under section 8.1 of the Fishing Regulations`

@export On what earnings is my rate of weekly benefits worked out as a fisher, in dollars (s 153.1923(1))?
GIVEN `the day on which I make my initial claim for benefits` IS A DATE @desc On what day do you make your initial claim for benefits? (a date)
      `my initial claim is made under subsection 8(6)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your initial claim made under subsection 8(6) of the Fishing Regulations (answer no if under subsection 8(1))?
      `there are earnings that would be used to calculate my rate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are there earnings that would be used to calculate your rate of weekly benefits?
      `the earnings that would be used to calculate my rate` IS A NUMBER @desc What are those earnings, in dollars? (0 if none)
      `I had an earlier benefit period of the first kind` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you have a benefit period established under subsection 8(1) (or 8(6) if you claim under 8(6)) in the earlier of the two periods the section names?
      `the day on which that earlier benefit period was established, the first kind` IS A DATE @desc On what day was that benefit period established? (a date; any date if none)
      `the earnings used for that earlier benefit period, the first kind` IS A NUMBER @desc What earnings were used to calculate your rate for it, in dollars? (0 if none)
      `I had an earlier benefit period of the second kind` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you have a benefit period established in the other of the two periods the section names?
      `the day on which that earlier benefit period was established, the second kind` IS A DATE @desc On what day was that benefit period established? (a date; any date if none)
      `the earnings used for that earlier benefit period, the second kind` IS A NUMBER @desc What earnings were used to calculate your rate for it, in dollars? (0 if none)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `On what earnings is my rate of weekly benefits worked out as a fisher` IS
    IF `my initial claim is made under subsection 8(6)`
    THEN `s 153.1923(1)(b) the earnings on which the rate of weekly benefits is calculated, for an initial claim under subsection 8(6)`
            (`ei6 seat sections 153.1922 to 153.1924 have not ceased to apply on the day` `the day on which I make my initial claim for benefits`)
            `the day on which I make my initial claim for benefits`
            `the current earnings`
            `the first earlier benefit period`
            `the second earlier benefit period`
    ELSE `s 153.1923(1)(a) the earnings on which the rate of weekly benefits is calculated, for an initial claim under subsection 8(1)`
            (`ei6 seat sections 153.1922 to 153.1924 have not ceased to apply on the day` `the day on which I make my initial claim for benefits`)
            `the current earnings`
            `the first earlier benefit period`
            `the second earlier benefit period`
    WHERE
        `the current earnings` MEANS IF `there are earnings that would be used to calculate my rate` THEN JUST `the earnings that would be used to calculate my rate` ELSE NOTHING
        `the first earlier benefit period` MEANS
            IF `I had an earlier benefit period of the first kind`
            THEN JUST (`ei6 Earlier benefit period of a fisher` OF `the day on which that earlier benefit period was established, the first kind`, `the earnings used for that earlier benefit period, the first kind`)
            ELSE NOTHING
        `the second earlier benefit period` MEANS
            IF `I had an earlier benefit period of the second kind`
            THEN JUST (`ei6 Earlier benefit period of a fisher` OF `the day on which that earlier benefit period was established, the second kind`, `the earnings used for that earlier benefit period, the second kind`)
            ELSE NOTHING

@export May a benefit period be established for me as a fisher under paragraph 153.1923(1)(a) (s 153.1923(2))?
GIVEN `the number of benefit periods already established for me under paragraph 153.1923(1)(a)` IS A NUMBER @desc How many benefit periods have already been established for you under paragraph 153.1923(1)(a)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May a benefit period be established for me as a fisher under paragraph 153.1923(1)(a)` IF
    `s 153.1923(2) a benefit period may be established for the fisher under paragraph (1)(a)` `the number of benefit periods already established for me under paragraph 153.1923(1)(a)`

@export May a benefit period be established for me as a fisher under paragraph 153.1923(1)(b) (s 153.1923(2))?
GIVEN `the number of benefit periods already established for me under paragraph 153.1923(1)(b)` IS A NUMBER @desc How many benefit periods have already been established for you under paragraph 153.1923(1)(b)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May a benefit period be established for me as a fisher under paragraph 153.1923(1)(b)` IF
    `s 153.1923(2) a benefit period may be established for the fisher under paragraph (1)(b)` `the number of benefit periods already established for me under paragraph 153.1923(1)(b)`

@export Do I qualify for special benefits as a fisher with at least $2,500 of insurable earnings (s 153.1925)?
GIVEN `the day on which I make my initial claim for benefits` IS A DATE @desc On what day do you make your initial claim for benefits? (a date)
      `I am an insured person who is not qualified to receive benefits under section 7` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an insured person who is not qualified to receive benefits under section 7?
      `I am claiming special benefits` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you claiming special benefits (sickness, maternity, parental or caring benefits)?
      `my insurable earnings from employment as a fisher in my qualifying period` IS A NUMBER @desc What are your insurable earnings from employment as a fisher in your qualifying period, in dollars?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do I qualify for special benefits as a fisher with at least $2,500 of insurable earnings` IF
    `s 153.1925 the insured person qualifies to receive the special benefits by this section`
        (`ei6 seat Part VIII.5 has not ceased to apply on the day` `the day on which I make my initial claim for benefits`)
        `I am an insured person who is not qualified to receive benefits under section 7`
        `I am claiming special benefits`
        `my insurable earnings from employment as a fisher in my qualifying period`

-- s 153.193. Earnings that are excluded from deductions.
@export Are this pay or these earnings excluded from the earnings deducted from my benefits (s 153.193(a))?
GIVEN `the first day of my benefit period` IS A DATE @desc On what day does your benefit period begin? (a date)
      `it is pay or earnings referred to in subsection 36(8), (9) or (19) of the Regulations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it pay or earnings referred to in subsection 36(8), (9) or (19) of the Employment Insurance Regulations?
      `the day on which I declared the pay or earnings to the Commission` IS A DATE @desc On what day did you declare the pay or earnings to the Commission? (a date)
      `the first day of the week to which they would otherwise be allocated` IS A DATE @desc What is the first day of the week to which they would otherwise be allocated under section 36 of the Regulations? (a date)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Are this pay or these earnings excluded from the earnings deducted from my benefits` IF
    `s 153.193(a) the pay or earnings are excluded from the earnings referred to in section 35 of the Regulations`
        (`ei6 seat Part VIII.5 has not ceased to apply on the day` `the first day of my benefit period`)
        `it is pay or earnings referred to in subsection 36(8), (9) or (19) of the Regulations`
        `the first day of my benefit period`
        `the day on which I declared the pay or earnings to the Commission`
        `the first day of the week to which they would otherwise be allocated`

@export How much of a payment for my first week is excluded from the earnings deducted from my benefits, in dollars (s 153.193(b))?
GIVEN `the first day of my benefit period` IS A DATE @desc On what day does your benefit period begin? (a date)
      `my waiting period has been waived under subsection 153.191(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has your waiting period been waived under subsection 153.191(1)?
      `the payment is for the first week for which benefits are payable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the payment paid to you as an insured person for the first week for which benefits are payable?
      `the payment is one referred to in subsection 38(1) rather than 37(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a payment referred to in subsection 38(1) of the Regulations? (answer no if it is one referred to in subsection 37(1))
      `the amount of the payment` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the amount of the payment, in dollars?
      `my normal weekly earnings from the employment to which the payment relates` IS A NUMBER @desc What are your normal weekly earnings from the employment to which the payment relates, in dollars?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `How much of a payment for my first week is excluded from the earnings deducted from my benefits` IS
    `s 153.193(b) the portion of the payment that is excluded from the earnings referred to in section 35 of the Regulations`
        (`ei6 seat Part VIII.5 has not ceased to apply on the day` `the first day of my benefit period`)
        `my waiting period has been waived under subsection 153.191(1)`
        `the payment is for the first week for which benefits are payable`
        (IF `the payment is one referred to in subsection 38(1) rather than 37(1)` THEN `ei6 a payment referred to in subsection 38(1) of the Regulations` ELSE `ei6 a payment referred to in subsection 37(1) of the Regulations`)
        `the amount of the payment`
        `my normal weekly earnings from the employment to which the payment relates`

-- s 153.194. Which employment counts for the disqualification and disentitlement sections 30 to 33.
@export Does this employment count for the disqualification and disentitlement rules of sections 30 to 33 (s 153.194)?
GIVEN `the first day of the employment` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the employment begin? (a date)
      `the last day of the employment` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the employment end? (a date)
      `the first day of my qualifying period` IS A DATE @desc What is the first day of your qualifying period? (a date)
      `the last day of my qualifying period` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day of your qualifying period? (a date)
      `the first day of my benefit period` IS A DATE @desc On what day does your benefit period begin? (a date)
      `the last day of my benefit period` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day of your benefit period? (a date)
      `the Sunday of the week in which my interruption of earnings occurred` IS A DATE @desc What is the Sunday of the week in which your interruption of earnings occurred? (a date)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does this employment count for the disqualification and disentitlement rules of sections 30 to 33` IF
    `s 153.194 the employment is employment for the purposes of sections 30 to 33`
        (`ei6 seat Part VIII.5 has not ceased to apply on the day` `the first day of my benefit period`)
        (`Period of days` OF `the first day of the employment`, `the last day of the employment`)
        (`Period of days` OF `the first day of my qualifying period`, `the last day of my qualifying period`)
        (`Period of days` OF `the first day of my benefit period`, `the last day of my benefit period`)
        `the Sunday of the week in which my interruption of earnings occurred`

-- s 153.195.
@export Is the Commission excused from giving me and my employer the opportunity to give information before it decides (s 153.195)?
GIVEN `the day on which I make my initial claim for benefits` IS A DATE @desc On what day do you make your initial claim for benefits? (a date)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the Commission excused from giving me and my employer the opportunity to give information before it decides` IF
    `s 153.195 the Commission is not required to give the claimant and the employer the opportunity referred to in paragraph 51(a)`
        (`ei6 seat Part VIII.5 has not ceased to apply on the day` `the day on which I make my initial claim for benefits`)

§ `Part VIII.6 - temporary measures (benefit periods beginning September 26 to November 20, 2021)`

-- The group applies only if your benefit period begins from September 26 to November 20, 2021.
@export What weekly insurable earnings are used for me, in dollars (s 153.197(1))?
GIVEN `the first day of my benefit period` IS A DATE @desc On what day does your benefit period begin? (a date)
      `my insurable earnings in the calculation period` IS A NUMBER @desc What were your insurable earnings in the calculation period of subsection 14(4), in dollars?
      `the number of weeks in that period in which I had insurable earnings` IS A NUMBER @desc In how many weeks of that period did you have insurable earnings?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `What weekly insurable earnings are used for me under Part VIII.6` IS
    `s 153.197(1) the weekly insurable earnings of the claimant are deemed to be` `the first day of my benefit period` `my insurable earnings in the calculation period` `the number of weeks in that period in which I had insurable earnings`

@export What weekly insurable earnings are used for me as a self-employed person under Part VIII.6, in dollars (s 153.197(2))?
GIVEN `the first day of my benefit period` IS A DATE @desc On what day does your benefit period begin? (a date)
      `the aggregate of my amounts under paragraphs 152.16(1)(a) and (b)` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the aggregate of the amounts referred to in paragraphs 152.16(1)(a) and (b), in dollars?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `What weekly insurable earnings are used for me as a self-employed person under Part VIII.6` IS
    `s 153.197(2) the result of dividing the aggregate by 52, for a self-employed person` `the first day of my benefit period` `the aggregate of my amounts under paragraphs 152.16(1)(a) and (b)`

@export What weekly insurable earnings are used for me as a fisher under Part VIII.6, in dollars (s 153.197(3))?
GIVEN `the first day of my benefit period` IS A DATE @desc On what day does your benefit period begin? (a date)
      `my weekly insurable earnings under paragraph 8.1(a) of the Fishing Regulations` IS A NUMBER @desc What are your weekly insurable earnings under paragraph 8.1(a) of the Employment Insurance (Fishing) Regulations, in dollars?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `What weekly insurable earnings are used for me as a fisher under Part VIII.6` IS
    `s 153.197(3) the weekly insurable earnings of the fisher are deemed to be` `the first day of my benefit period` `my weekly insurable earnings under paragraph 8.1(a) of the Fishing Regulations`

§ `Part IX - transitional provisions and coming into force`

-- The group applies only if your claim, allowance or employment goes back to before June 30, 1996, or you ask about the
-- days on which the Act's provisions came into force: ask "Did this happen to you?" first.

-- s 156, s 157, s 165.
@export May my training allowance under the National Training Act continue to be paid (s 156)?
GIVEN `it was being paid to me under section 5 of the National Training Act when that Act was repealed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was a training allowance being paid to you under section 5 of the National Training Act when that Act was repealed?
      `the course to which the allowance relates has concluded` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the course to which the allowance relates concluded?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May my training allowance under the National Training Act continue to be paid` IF
    `s 156 the training allowance may continue to be paid in accordance with the National Training Act` `it was being paid to me under section 5 of the National Training Act when that Act was repealed` `the course to which the allowance relates has concluded`

@export Does my agreement under section 7 of the National Training Act continue in effect (s 157)?
GIVEN `it was in effect when that Act was repealed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your agreement under section 7 of the National Training Act in effect when that Act was repealed?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does my agreement under section 7 of the National Training Act continue in effect` IF
    `s 157 the agreement continues in effect according to its terms` `it was in effect when that Act was repealed`

@export Does my waiver or agreement under paragraph 4(1)(d) of the former Act continue in effect (s 165)?
GIVEN `it was in effect when the former Act was repealed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your waiver or agreement under paragraph 4(1)(d) of the Unemployment Insurance Act in effect when that Act was repealed?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does my waiver or agreement under paragraph 4(1)(d) of the former Act continue in effect` IF
    `s 165 the waiver or agreement continues in effect as though made under paragraph 5(4)(d) of this Act` `it was in effect when the former Act was repealed`

-- s 159. The old Unemployment Insurance Act and this Act.
@export Are the matters relating to my claim dealt with under the old Unemployment Insurance Act (s 159(1))?
GIVEN `the first day of my benefit period` IS A DATE @desc On what day did your benefit period begin? (a date)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Are the matters relating to my claim dealt with under the old Unemployment Insurance Act` IF
    `s 159(1) the Act under which matters relating to the claim are dealt with` `the first day of my benefit period` EQUALS `ei6 the former Act (the Unemployment Insurance Act)`

@export May the Tax Court of Canada decide my appeal under the old Act without giving written reasons (s 159(1.01))?
GIVEN `my appeal is under the former Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your appeal under the Unemployment Insurance Act (the former Act)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the Tax Court of Canada decide my appeal under the old Act without giving written reasons` IF
    `s 159(1.01) the Tax Court of Canada need not give reasons in writing for its decision` `my appeal is under the former Act`

@export Does subsection 19(3) apply to my failure to declare earnings (s 159(1.1))?
GIVEN `the first day of the period in which I failed to declare earnings` IS A DATE @desc What is the first day of the period, determined under the regulations, in which you failed to declare earnings? (a date)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does subsection 19(3) apply to my failure to declare earnings` IF
    `s 159(1.1) subsection 19(3) applies to the claimant` `the first day of the period in which I failed to declare earnings`

@export May the Commission deduct from my benefits for earnings I failed to declare (s 159(1.1))?
GIVEN `the day of the deduction` IS A DATE @desc On what day would the deduction be made? (a date)
      `the first day of the period in which I failed to declare earnings` IS A DATE @desc What is the first day of the period in which you failed to declare earnings? (a date)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the Commission deduct from my benefits for earnings I failed to declare` IF
    `s 159(1.1) the Commission may make a deduction under subparagraph 19(3)(a)(i)` `the day of the deduction` `the first day of the period in which I failed to declare earnings`

@export Does subsection 19(4) apply to me because I began a course or program after the former Act was repealed (s 159(1.2))?
GIVEN `the day on which I began attending the course or program` IS A DATE @desc On what day did you begin attending the course or program? (a date)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does subsection 19(4) apply to me because I began a course or program after the former Act was repealed` IF
    `s 159(1.2) subsection 19(4) applies to the claimant` `the day on which I began attending the course or program`

@export Does section 23 apply to me in place of section 20 of the former Act (s 159(2))?
GIVEN `the day on which my child was born or placed with me for adoption` IS A DATE @desc On what day was your child born or placed with you for adoption? (a date)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does section 23 apply to me in place of section 20 of the former Act` IF
    `s 159(2) section 23 applies in place of section 20 of the former Act` `the day on which my child was born or placed with me for adoption`

@export Does section 25 of the former Act still apply to me (s 159(3))?
GIVEN `I was employed on a job creation project under section 25 of the former Act when that Act was repealed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you employed on a job creation project under section 25 of the Unemployment Insurance Act when that Act was repealed?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does section 25 of the former Act still apply to me` IF
    `s 159(3) section 25 of the former Act applies to the claimant` `I was employed on a job creation project under section 25 of the former Act when that Act was repealed`

@export Does section 26 of the former Act still apply to me (s 159(4))?
GIVEN `I was in a course or program to which I was referred under section 26 of the former Act before that Act was repealed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you in a course or program to which you were referred under section 26 of the Unemployment Insurance Act before that Act was repealed?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does section 26 of the former Act still apply to me` IF
    `s 159(4) section 26 of the former Act applies to the claimant` `I was in a course or program to which I was referred under section 26 of the former Act before that Act was repealed`

@export Do sections 27 to 33 of this Act apply to my disentitlement or disqualification (s 159(6))?
GIVEN `the day of the event that gave rise to the disentitlement or disqualification` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the event that gave rise to the disentitlement or disqualification occur? (a date)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do sections 27 to 33 of this Act apply to my disentitlement or disqualification` IF
    `s 159(6) sections 27 to 33 apply in place of sections 27 to 28.3 of the former Act` `the day of the event that gave rise to the disentitlement or disqualification`

@export Which section of this Act is a reference in the former Act to a section read as (s 159(6))?
GIVEN `the number of the section of the former Act` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the number of the section of the former Act? (27, 28, 28.1, 28.2 or 28.3)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Which section of this Act is a reference in the former Act to a section read as` IS
    `s 159(6) the section of this Act that a reference in the former Act is read as a reference to` `the number of the section of the former Act`

@export Does section 145 apply to the benefits paid to me (s 159(7))?
GIVEN `the day on which the benefits were paid to me` IS A DATE @desc On what day were the benefits paid to you? (a date)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does section 145 apply to the benefits paid to me` IF
    `s 159(7) section 145 applies in place of section 123 of the former Act` `the day on which the benefits were paid to me`

-- s 160, s 161.
@export Which law determines my hours of insurable employment and insurable earnings from before 1997 (s 160)?
GIVEN `the Part under which I claim` IS A `Part of the Act` @desc Under which Part of the Act do you claim benefits?
      `the day on which my insurable employment and insurable earnings occurred` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the insurable employment and insurable earnings occur? (a date)
GIVETH A MAYBE `ei6 Law that determines insurable employment and insurable earnings before 1997`
DECIDE `Which law determines my hours of insurable employment and insurable earnings from before 1997` IS
    `s 160 the law that determines the hours of insurable employment and the insurable earnings` `the Part under which I claim` `the day on which my insurable employment and insurable earnings occurred`

@export Is a matter about the payment of premiums under the former Act dealt with under that Act (s 161)?
GIVEN `the matter relates to the payment of premiums under the former Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the matter relate to the payment of premiums under the Unemployment Insurance Act?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is a matter about the payment of premiums under the former Act dealt with under that Act` IF
    `s 161 the matter is dealt with under the former Act` `the matter relates to the payment of premiums under the former Act`

-- s 190. The days on which provisions came into force, and Schedule II.
@export On what day did a provision of the Act as enacted come into force (s 190)?
GIVEN `the provision` IS A STRING @desc Name the provision as section 190 does, for example "section 4", "subsection 5(6)", "paragraph 90(1)(d)", "section 7", "Schedule I" or "section 173"
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `On what day did a provision of the Act as enacted come into force` IS
    `s 190 the day on which the provision comes into force` `the provision`

@export May the Commission take into account a notice issued under subsection 7.1(4) on or after June 30, 1996 (s 190(3.1))?
GIVEN `the day on which the notice was issued` IS A DATE @desc On what day was the notice under subsection 7.1(4) issued? (a date)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the Commission take into account a notice issued under subsection 7.1(4) on or after June 30, 1996` IF
    `s 190(3.1) the Commission may take the notice into account in applying subsections 7.1(1) to (3)` `the day on which the notice was issued`

@export May the Commission deduct for earnings I did not declare for a period beginning on or after June 30, 1996 (s 190(3.2))?
GIVEN `the day of the deduction` IS A DATE @desc On what day would the deduction be made? (a date)
      `the first day of the period for which I did not declare earnings` IS A DATE @desc What is the first day of the period for which you did not declare earnings? (a date)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the Commission deduct for earnings I did not declare for a period beginning on or after June 30, 1996` IF
    `s 190(3.2) the Commission may make a deduction under subparagraph 19(3)(a)(i)` `the day of the deduction` `the first day of the period for which I did not declare earnings`

@export Did Schedule II apply in place of this provision on this day (s 190(4))?
GIVEN `the provision` IS A STRING @desc Name the provision as section 190 does, for example "section 4", "section 7", "subsection 12(2)" or "section 14"
      `the day` IS A DATE @desc On what day do you want the answer for? (a date)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Did Schedule II apply in place of this provision on this day` IF
    `s 190(4) Schedule II applies in place of the provision on the day` `the provision` `the day`

@export Does paragraph 6 of Schedule II continue to apply to me in place of sections 14, 16 and 17 (s 190(5))?
GIVEN `the first day of my benefit period` IS A DATE @desc On what day did your benefit period begin? (a date)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does paragraph 6 of Schedule II continue to apply to me in place of sections 14, 16 and 17` IF
    `s 190(5) paragraph 6 of Schedule II continues to apply in place of sections 14, 16 and 17` `the first day of my benefit period`

§ `Schedule I, Schedule IV, Schedule V and Schedule VI - the tables`

@export How many weeks of regular benefits can I be paid at most (Schedule I, s 12(2))?
GIVEN `my hours of insurable employment in my qualifying period` IS A NUMBER @desc How many hours of insurable employment do you have in your qualifying period? (whole hours)
      `the regional rate of unemployment that applies to me, in per cent` IS A NUMBER @desc What regional rate of unemployment applies to you, in per cent? (7.5 for 7.5%)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `How many weeks of regular benefits can I be paid at most` IS
    `Act Schedule I the maximum number of weeks of benefits` `my hours of insurable employment in my qualifying period` (`the regional rate of unemployment that applies to me, in per cent` DIVIDED BY 100)

@export How many weeks of regular benefits can I be paid at most as a seasonal worker (Schedule V, s 12(2.3))?
GIVEN `my hours of insurable employment in my qualifying period` IS A NUMBER @desc How many hours of insurable employment do you have in your qualifying period? (whole hours)
      `the regional rate of unemployment that applies to me, in per cent` IS A NUMBER @desc What regional rate of unemployment applies to you, in per cent? (7.5 for 7.5%)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `How many weeks of regular benefits can I be paid at most as a seasonal worker` IS
    `Act Schedule V the maximum number of weeks of benefits for seasonal workers` `my hours of insurable employment in my qualifying period` (`the regional rate of unemployment that applies to me, in per cent` DIVIDED BY 100)

@export How many weeks of benefits at the 55% rate do my weeks of extended parental benefits count as (Schedule IV, s 12(7))?
GIVEN `the weeks of benefits paid to me under the 61-week maximum` IS A NUMBER @desc For how many weeks have benefits been paid to you for the care of a new-born or adopted child, where you elected the 61-week maximum? (whole weeks)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `How many weeks of benefits at the 55% rate do my weeks of extended parental benefits count as` IS
    `Act Schedule IV the number of weeks of benefits that would have been paid at a rate of weekly benefits of 55%` `the weeks of benefits paid to me under the 61-week maximum`

@export Which seasonal-worker region of Schedule VI is my home in (Schedule VI)?
GIVEN `my province or territory` IS A `ei6 Province or territory of Schedule VI` @desc In which province or territory do you live? (Quebec, Nova Scotia, New Brunswick, Prince Edward Island, Newfoundland/Labrador, Yukon, or another)
      `my census division number` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the number of your census division, in the 1996 Standard Geographical Classification? (0 if you do not know it)
      `my census subdivision number` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the number of your census subdivision? (the 1996 classification for New Brunswick and Newfoundland/Labrador, the 2011 classification for Prince Edward Island and Yukon; 0 if you do not know it)
      `the census metropolitan area or census agglomeration my home is part of` IS A `ei6 Area of Schedule VI` @desc Is your home part of one of these census metropolitan areas or census agglomerations?
GIVETH A `ei6 Region of Schedule VI`
DECIDE `Which seasonal-worker region of Schedule VI is my home in` IS
    `Schedule VI the region the place is in`
        (`ei6 Place for Schedule VI` OF `my province or territory`, `my census division number`, `my census subdivision number`, `the census metropolitan area or census agglomeration my home is part of`)

§ `Schedule II - the interim provisions (June 30, 1996 to January 5, 1997)`

-- The group applies only if your claim or employment falls between June 30, 1996 and January 5, 1997: ask "Did this
-- happen to you?" first. Each question asks for the day it is about and checks Schedule II applied on it (s 190(4)).

@export What was the maximum yearly insurable earnings for 1996 (Schedule II, paragraph 1)?
GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE @desc On what day do you want the answer for? (a date)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `What was the maximum yearly insurable earnings for 1996` IS
    `Schedule II para 1 s 4(1) the maximum yearly insurable earnings` `the day`

@export What was the maximum weekly insurable earnings (Schedule II, paragraph 1)?
GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE @desc On what day do you want the answer for? (a date)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `What was the maximum weekly insurable earnings` IS
    `Schedule II para 1 s 4(2) the maximum weekly insurable earnings` `the day`

@export Was I a major or a minor attachment claimant under the interim definitions (Schedule II, paragraph 3)?
GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE @desc On what day do you want the answer for? (a date)
      `I qualify to receive benefits` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you qualify to receive benefits?
      `my weeks of insurable employment in my qualifying period` IS A NUMBER @desc How many weeks of insurable employment do you have in your qualifying period?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Was I a major attachment claimant under the interim definitions` IF
    `Schedule II para 3 major attachment claimant` `the day` `I qualify to receive benefits` `my weeks of insurable employment in my qualifying period`

@export Do I qualify to receive benefits under the interim section 7 (Schedule II, paragraph 4)?
GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE @desc On what day do you want the answer for? (a date)
      `I have had an interruption of earnings from employment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you had an interruption of earnings from employment?
      `my weeks of insurable employment in my qualifying period` IS A NUMBER @desc How many weeks of insurable employment do you have in your qualifying period?
      `the regional rate of unemployment that applies to me, in per cent` IS A NUMBER @desc What regional rate of unemployment applies to you, in per cent? (7.5 for 7.5%)
      `my weeks of insurable employment in the last 52 weeks before my qualifying period` IS A NUMBER @desc How many weeks of insurable employment did you have in the last 52 weeks before your qualifying period?
      `my weeks of benefits paid or payable in those 52 weeks` IS A NUMBER @desc How many weeks in those 52 weeks had benefits paid or payable to you (not counting a week already counted)?
      `my prescribed weeks relating to employment in the labour force in those 52 weeks` IS A NUMBER @desc How many prescribed weeks relating to employment in the labour force did you have in those 52 weeks (not counting a week already counted)?
      `it is jointly determined that I must first exhaust benefit rights under the laws of another jurisdiction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has it been jointly determined that you must first exhaust or terminate benefit rights under the laws of another jurisdiction, as Article VI of the Canada-United States agreement of 1942 provides?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do I qualify to receive benefits under the interim section 7` IF
        `Schedule II para 4 s 7(2) and (3) the insured person qualifies to receive benefits`
            `the day`
            (`Schedule II para 4 s 7(4) the insured person is a new entrant or a re-entrant to the labour force` `the day` `my weeks of insurable employment in the last 52 weeks before my qualifying period` `my weeks of benefits paid or payable in those 52 weeks` `my prescribed weeks relating to employment in the labour force in those 52 weeks`)
            `I have had an interruption of earnings from employment`
            `my weeks of insurable employment in my qualifying period`
            (`the regional rate of unemployment that applies to me, in per cent` DIVIDED BY 100)
    AND NOT (`Schedule II para 4 s 7(6) the claimant is not qualified to receive benefits` `the day` `it is jointly determined that I must first exhaust benefit rights under the laws of another jurisdiction`)

@export How many weeks of benefits can I be paid at most under the interim Schedule I (Schedule II, paragraphs 5 and 18)?
GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE @desc On what day do you want the answer for? (a date)
      `my weeks of insurable employment in my qualifying period` IS A NUMBER @desc How many weeks of insurable employment do you have in your qualifying period? (whole weeks)
      `the regional rate of unemployment that applies to me, in per cent` IS A NUMBER @desc What regional rate of unemployment applies to you, in per cent? (7.5 for 7.5%)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `How many weeks of benefits can I be paid at most under the interim Schedule I` IS
    `Schedule II para 5 s 12(2) the maximum number of weeks for which benefits may be paid in a benefit period` `the day` `my weeks of insurable employment in my qualifying period` (`the regional rate of unemployment that applies to me, in per cent` DIVIDED BY 100)

@export What is my rate of weekly benefits under the interim section 14, in dollars (Schedule II, paragraph 6)?
GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE @desc On what day do you want the answer for? (a date)
      `the first day of my benefit period` IS A DATE @desc On what day did your benefit period begin? (a date)
      `I am a major attachment claimant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a major attachment claimant (20 or more weeks of insurable employment in your qualifying period)?
      `my insurable earnings in the last 20 weeks of insurable employment in my qualifying period` IS A NUMBER @desc What are your insurable earnings in the last 20 weeks of insurable employment in your qualifying period, in dollars?
      `my insurable earnings in my qualifying period` IS A NUMBER @desc What are your insurable earnings in your whole qualifying period, in dollars?
      `my weeks of insurable employment in my qualifying period` IS A NUMBER @desc How many weeks of insurable employment do you have in your qualifying period?
      `the regional rate of unemployment that applies to me, in per cent` IS A NUMBER @desc What regional rate of unemployment applies to you, in per cent? (7.5 for 7.5%)
      `I have dependants, or the Commission is of the opinion that I or my spouse support dependants` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it established that the prescribed circumstances exist in relation to dependants of you or your spouse, or is the Commission of the opinion that you or your spouse support dependants?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `What is my rate of weekly benefits under the interim section 14` IS
    CONSIDER `my average weekly insurable earnings`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST earnings THEN `Schedule II para 6 s 14(1) the rate of weekly benefits` `Schedule II paragraph 6 applies` earnings `I have dependants, or the Commission is of the opinion that I or my spouse support dependants`
    WHERE
        `Schedule II paragraph 6 applies` MEANS
            `Schedule II para 6 applies in place of sections 14, 16 and 17` `the day` `the first day of my benefit period`
        `my average weekly insurable earnings` MEANS
            IF `I am a major attachment claimant`
            THEN `Schedule II para 6 s 14(2) the average weekly insurable earnings of a major attachment claimant` `Schedule II paragraph 6 applies` `my insurable earnings in the last 20 weeks of insurable employment in my qualifying period`
            ELSE `Schedule II para 6 s 14(3) the average weekly insurable earnings of a minor attachment claimant` `Schedule II paragraph 6 applies` `my insurable earnings in my qualifying period` `my weeks of insurable employment in my qualifying period` (`the regional rate of unemployment that applies to me, in per cent` DIVIDED BY 100)

@export How much is deducted from my benefits for a week because of my earnings, in dollars (Schedule II, paragraph 7)?
GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE @desc On what day do you want the answer for? (a date)
      `my earnings during the week` IS A NUMBER @desc What were your earnings during the week, in dollars?
      `my weekly rate of benefit` IS A NUMBER @desc What is your weekly rate of benefit, in dollars?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `How much is deducted from my benefits for a week because of my earnings` IS
    `Schedule II para 7 s 19(2) the amount deducted from the benefits payable for the week` `the day` `my earnings during the week` `my weekly rate of benefit`

@export Are weeks of disqualification not carried forward against me (Schedule II, paragraph 8)?
GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE @desc On what day do you want the answer for? (a date)
      `my weeks of insurable employment since the event giving rise to the disqualification` IS A NUMBER @desc How many weeks of insurable employment have you had since the event giving rise to the disqualification?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Are weeks of disqualification not carried forward against me` IF
    `Schedule II para 8 s 28(4) no weeks of disqualification are carried forward against the claimant` `the day` `my weeks of insurable employment since the event giving rise to the disqualification`

@export Have I been employed long enough since losing or leaving my employment to avoid disqualification (Schedule II, paragraph 9(1))?
GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE @desc On what day do you want the answer for? (a date)
      `my weeks of insurable employment since losing or leaving the employment` IS A NUMBER @desc How many weeks of insurable employment have you had since losing or leaving the employment?
      `the number of weeks required by section 7 to qualify for benefits` IS A NUMBER @desc How many weeks does section 7 require for you to qualify for benefits?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Have I been employed long enough since losing or leaving my employment to avoid disqualification` IF
    `Schedule II para 9(1) s 30(1)(a) the claimant has been employed in insurable employment for the number of weeks required by section 7` `the day` `my weeks of insurable employment since losing or leaving the employment` `the number of weeks required by section 7 to qualify for benefits`

@export May these weeks of insurable employment not be used to qualify for benefits (Schedule II, paragraph 9(2), s 30(5))?
GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE @desc On what day do you want the answer for? (a date)
      `they are weeks from that or any other employment before the day I lost or left it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are they weeks of insurable employment from that or any other employment before the day on which you lost or left that employment?
      `they are weeks in an employment I later lose or leave as described in subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are they weeks of insurable employment in an employment that you later lose or leave, as subsection 30(1) describes?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May these weeks of insurable employment not be used to qualify for benefits` IF
    `Schedule II para 9(2) s 30(5) the weeks may not be used for the purposes of subsection 7(2) or (3)` `the day` `they are weeks from that or any other employment before the day I lost or left it` `they are weeks in an employment I later lose or leave as described in subsection (1)`

@export May these weeks of insurable employment not be used for the number of weeks or the rate of my benefits (Schedule II, paragraph 9(2), s 30(6))?
