@export How much employee's premium must I pay for a week, in dollars (Schedule II, paragraph 13)?
GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE @desc On what day do you want the answer for? (a date)
      `I am employed in insurable employment during the week` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you employed in insurable employment during the week?
      `my insurable earnings for the week` IS A NUMBER @desc What are your insurable earnings for the week, in dollars?
      `the percentage the Commission fixed as the employee's premium for the year, in per cent` IS A NUMBER @desc What percentage did the Commission fix as the employee's premium for the year, in per cent? (2.95 for 2.95%)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `How much employee's premium must I pay for a week` IS
    `Schedule II para 13 s 67(1) the employee's premium for the week` `the day` `I am employed in insurable employment during the week` `my insurable earnings for the week` (`the percentage the Commission fixed as the employee's premium for the year, in per cent` DIVIDED BY 100)

